{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Of the fowl after their kind</b>: The word יבאו אליך means they will come of themselves; he need not exert himself to seek them on the islands or to hunt every species of fowl. And He commanded him to prepare food of every kind for all. The wandering of spirit will ask: what did every bird of prey eat, and every beast such as the lion, which does not live except from flesh? This is no question, for one who finds no meat will eat grass and the fruit of the tree when he hungers. So too it was expounded that among the beasts there is one great creature, and it is 'the roe of a thousand hills' (Psalm 50:10) — it is good for the listening ear. And likewise a bird that covers the light of the sun with its wings — there is a sod to it, and it is not as it sounds. And HaShem commanded Noah to make the ark many days before the Flood came, and when the days drew near, the honored HaShem commanded that Noah and his household go into the ark. And on account of the need for an offering, the honored HaShem commanded that he take from the pure beast and from the pure fowl, seven males and seven females."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:36.709680784Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}